fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Harvest"
letter: "H"
anchor: "harvest"
category: "growing"
---

The process of cutting cannabis plants at the end of the flowering stage to collect the mature buds. Harvest timing is one of the most important decisions in home growing — harvesting too early reduces potency and yield; harvesting too late shifts the effect profile toward more sedating as THC degrades to CBN. Trichome colour is the most reliable harvest timing indicator: mostly cloudy/milky trichomes indicate peak THC; increasing amber indicates THC degradation and a more sedative effect.
